[statement]
A package that two removals free goes after the other packages the first
of them needs: `x` needs `a`, `b` and `c`, and `a` needs `c` too. apk
removes `x`, `a`, `b`, then `c`, not `c` right after `a`. Contrast
`freed-packages-are-removed-depth-first`, where only `l1` needs `l3`.

[repository]
P:n
V:1

[installed]
P:c
V:1

P:a
V:1
D:c

P:b
V:1

P:x
V:1
D:a b c

[request]
n

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove x 1
remove a 1
remove b 1
remove c 1
install n 1
